    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73764" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμονο-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be of one mind, agree,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στασιάζω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				8.75
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				2.63
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔθ᾽ οἱ τρόποι γὰρ ὁμονοοῦσ᾽ οὔθ᾽
					οἱ νόμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anaxandr.
					39.2
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-οῦσα ὀλιγαρχία</span> a
				<i>united</i> oligarchy, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στασιάζουσα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1306a9
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεις -οῦσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Rh.Al.</u>
					1422b35
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συγγενείας -ούσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Sent.Vat.</u>
					61
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀμονόεντες</span> (
				Aeol.
			
			part.) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς ἀλλάλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12(2).6.30
				</span></i>
			(Mytil.) ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. ὅτι . . </span>
			<i>to be agreed</i> that . . , <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Men.</u>
				86c
			</span></i> : c. neut. Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπειδὴ ὁμονοοῦμεν ταῦτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					4.2.47
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ τῶν ἄλλων ὁ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					9.53
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat.,
				<i>live in harmony with,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					And.
					1.108
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				352a
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ. τινὶ περί τινος</span>
			<i>to be of one mind</i> with him about . . , <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1.126c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				4.85
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1167a29
				</span></i>
			 : metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλὸς ὁμονοεῖ
			χοροῖς</span> Diog.Trag.<i><span class="en">
				1.11
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτυχία ὁ. τοῖς κινδύνοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					2.43
				</span></i>
			 ; of drugs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῖ τὰ καθαρτικὰ μιγνύμενα ὁμονοεῖν
					ἀλλήλοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					16.117
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁμονοοῦσαι,</span> term applied
			to the Muses by <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				222
			</span></i>.</div>
